        <mxCell id="c233" value="Design Services&#x27;s row, zero in every month" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="306" y="608" width="241.692" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c234" value="&lt;i&gt;Report editor, page Ex C.2, fiscal 2026 chosen on the tile slicer. The matrix has no total row or column, and the line chart is in month order. Design Services reads 0.00 in every month because it has invoice lines every month and each has a discount of zero. Design Trade peaks in November, with its own promotion; the others peak in September or October, with the autumn promotion. The real toolbar shows icons, and the real editor shows the Filters and Visualizations panes beside Data: the mock writes the toolbar&#x27;s names and draws the Data pane as an inset, because twelve months of amounts to the cent need the full width.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="636" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
